<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Sovereignty — Who Controls the Layer Below You</title>
<script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/fontsource/fonts/jetbrains-mono@latest/latin-400-normal.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/fontsource/fonts/inter@latest/latin-400-normal.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/fontsource/fonts/inter@latest/latin-700-normal.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/fontsource/fonts/playfair-display@latest/latin-700-normal.css">
<style>
:root {
  --bg: #0a0a0b;
  --surface: #111113;
  --border: #1e1e22;
  --text: #e8e6e3;
  --text-dim: #8a8a8e;
  --amber: #f59e0b;
  --cyan: #06b6d4;
  --emerald: #10b981;
  --crimson: #ef4444;
  --violet: #8b5cf6;
  --sky: #38bdf8;
}

* { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }

html {
  scroll-behavior: smooth;
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--text);
}

body {
  font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  line-height: 1.7;
  overflow-x: hidden;
}

.font-mono { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; }
.font-display { font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif; }

/* Scrollbar */
::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 4px; }
::-webkit-scrollbar-track { background: var(--bg); }
::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb { background: #333; border-radius: 2px; }

/* Layer indicator */
.layer-nav {
  position: fixed;
  right: 24px;
  top: 50%;
  transform: translateY(-50%);
  z-index: 100;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 12px;
}

.layer-dot {
  width: 10px;
  height: 10px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  border: 1.5px solid #444;
  background: transparent;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: all 0.4s ease;
  position: relative;
}

.layer-dot.active {
  transform: scale(1.4);
  border-color: currentColor;
  background: currentColor;
  box-shadow: 0 0 12px currentColor;
}

.layer-dot::after {
  content: attr(data-label);
  position: absolute;
  right: 20px;
  top: 50%;
  transform: translateY(-50%);
  white-space: nowrap;
  font-size: 11px;
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  color: #666;
  opacity: 0;
  transition: opacity 0.3s;
  pointer-events: none;
}

.layer-dot:hover::after,
.layer-dot.active::after {
  opacity: 1;
  color: var(--text-dim);
}

/* Section styles */
.section-block {
  min-height: 100vh;
  padding: 120px 0;
  position: relative;
}

.section-block::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
  height: 1px;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--border), transparent);
}

/* Hero */
.hero {
  min-height: 100vh;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.hero-grid {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  background-image: 
    linear-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,0.02) 1px, transparent 1px),
    linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.02) 1px, transparent 1px);
  background-size: 60px 60px;
}

.hero-glow {
  position: absolute;
  width: 600px;
  height: 600px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  filter: blur(120px);
  opacity: 0.15;
  animation: pulse 8s ease-in-out infinite;
}

@keyframes pulse {
  0%, 100% { transform: scale(1); opacity: 0.15; }
  50% { transform: scale(1.2); opacity: 0.25; }
}

/* Content */
.content-wrapper {
  max-width: 720px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 0 24px;
}

.prose-section p {
  margin-bottom: 1.5em;
  color: var(--text);
  font-size: 16px;
}

.prose-section strong {
  color: #fff;
  font-weight: 700;
}

.prose-section .highlight {
  color: var(--amber);
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 14px;
}

/* Stat cards */
.stat-card {
  background: var(--surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 8px;
  padding: 20px;
  transition: all 0.3s ease;
}

.stat-card:hover {
  border-color: #333;
  transform: translateY(-2px);
}

/* Diagram containers */
.diagram-container {
  background: var(--surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 12px;
  padding: 32px;
  margin: 40px 0;
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.diagram-container::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
  height: 2px;
}

/* Bullet points */
.tech-bullet {
  padding: 16px 20px;
  background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02);
  border-left: 2px solid;
  margin: 16px 0;
  border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
}

/* Reveal animation */
.reveal {
  opacity: 0;
  transform: translateY(30px);
  transition: all 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
}

.reveal.visible {
  opacity: 1;
  transform: translateY(0);
}

/* Section number */
.section-number {
  font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
  font-size: 120px;
  font-weight: 700;
  line-height: 1;
  opacity: 0.06;
  position: absolute;
  top: 60px;
  left: -20px;
}

/* Quote block */
.quote-block {
  border-left: 3px solid;
  padding: 24px 32px;
  margin: 40px 0;
  background: rgba(255,255,255,0.01);
  font-style: italic;
  font-size: 18px;
  line-height: 1.8;
}

/* Layer stack visualization */
.layer-stack-viz {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 4px;
  margin: 40px 0;
}

.layer-bar {
  height: 40px;
  border-radius: 4px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  padding: 0 16px;
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 12px;
  transition: all 0.5s ease;
  cursor: pointer;
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.layer-bar::after {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(255,255,255,0.05));
  opacity: 0;
  transition: opacity 0.3s;
}

.layer-bar:hover::after { opacity: 1; }

.layer-bar.active {
  transform: scaleX(1.02);
  box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
}

/* Chiplet diagram */
.chiplet-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
  gap: 6px;
  max-width: 400px;
  margin: 0 auto;
}

.chiplet {
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  border-radius: 4px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 10px;
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  transition: all 0.3s;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.chiplet:hover {
  transform: scale(1.1);
  z-index: 2;
}

/* Ring diagram */
.ring-diagram {
  position: relative;
  width: 300px;
  height: 300px;
  margin: 0 auto;
}

.ring {
  position: absolute;
  border-radius: 50%;
  border: 2px solid;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  transition: all 0.3s;
}

/* Atmospheric layers */
.atmo-layers {
  position: relative;
  height: 400px;
  border-radius: 12px;
  overflow: hidden;
}

/* Synthesis */
.synthesis-line {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 12px;
  padding: 12px 16px;
  border-radius: 6px;
  margin: 8px 0;
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 13px;
  transition: all 0.3s;
  background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02);
}

.synthesis-line:hover {
  background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
  transform: translateX(8px);
}

.synthesis-dot {
  width: 8px;
  height: 8px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  flex-shrink: 0;
}

/* Canvas background */
#bg-canvas {
  position: fixed;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  z-index: -1;
  opacity: 0.4;
}

/* Progress bar */
.progress-bar {
  position: fixed;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  height: 2px;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--amber), var(--cyan), var(--emerald), var(--crimson), var(--violet), var(--sky));
  z-index: 1000;
  transition: width 0.1s;
}

/* Mobile */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .layer-nav { display: none; }
  .section-number { font-size: 80px; }
  .content-wrapper { padding: 0 16px; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="progress-bar" id="progressBar"></div>
<canvas id="bg-canvas"></canvas>

<!-- Layer Navigation -->
<nav class="layer-nav" id="layerNav">
  <div class="layer-dot" data-label="00 — ORIGIN" data-section="hero" style="color: #fff;"></div>
  <div class="layer-dot" data-label="01 — PHYSICAL BOX" data-section="sec1" style="color: var(--amber);"></div>
  <div class="layer-dot" data-label="02 — SILICON" data-section="sec2" style="color: var(--cyan);"></div>
  <div class="layer-dot" data-label="03 — NATION" data-section="sec3" style="color: var(--emerald);"></div>
  <div class="layer-dot" data-label="04 — RING ZERO" data-section="sec4" style="color: var(--crimson);"></div>
  <div class="layer-dot" data-label="05 — CLOUD LEAKS" data-section="sec5" style="color: var(--violet);"></div>
  <div class="layer-dot" data-label="06 — THE AIR" data-section="sec6" style="color: var(--sky);"></div>
  <div class="layer-dot" data-label="∞ — SYNTHESIS" data-section="synthesis" style="color: #fff;"></div>
</nav>

<!-- HERO -->
<section class="hero" id="hero">
  <div class="hero-grid"></div>
  <div class="hero-glow" style="background: radial-gradient(circle, var(--amber), transparent); top: 20%; left: 30%;"></div>
  <div class="hero-glow" style="background: radial-gradient(circle, var(--cyan), transparent); bottom: 20%; right: 30%; animation-delay: -4s;"></div>
  
  <div class="content-wrapper text-center relative z-10">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase mb-6" style="color: var(--text-dim);">A Technical Essay in Six Layers</p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-5xl md:text-7xl font-bold mb-8 leading-tight">
      Sovereignty
    </h1>
    <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl mb-4" style="color: var(--text-dim);">
      Who controls the layer below you?
    </p>
    <p class="font-mono text-sm mt-12" style="color: #444;">
      ↓ scroll to descend
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION 1: THE PHYSICAL BOX -->
<section class="section-block" id="sec1">
  <div class="content-wrapper relative">
    <div class="section-number" style="color: var(--amber);">01</div>
    
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4" style="color: var(--amber);">Layer 01 — Hardware</p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-8">The Physical Box Is an Illusion</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-section reveal">
      <p>Most premium laptops you pay thousands for were never engineered by the brand on the lid. They are <strong>ODMs</strong> — Original Design Manufacturers.</p>
      
      <p><strong>Clevo</strong> is the textbook case. Founded in Taiwan in 1983, no retail stores, only barebones chassis: board, cooling module, shell. Brands like <strong>XMG</strong>, <strong>Sager</strong>, <strong>System76</strong> are VARs — Value Added Resellers. Clevo pours the concrete foundation, the VAR picks the paint and puts its mailbox out front.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="diagram-container reveal" style="--accent: var(--amber);">
      <div style="position:absolute;top:0;left:0;right:0;height:2px;background:var(--amber);"></div>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider mb-6" style="color:var(--amber);">ODM → VAR Supply Chain</p>
      <div class="layer-stack-viz">
        <div class="layer-bar" style="background:rgba(245,158,11,0.15);border:1px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.3);color:var(--amber);">
          CLEVO — Barebones: Board + Cooling + Shell
        </div>
        <div class="layer-bar" style="background:rgba(245,158,11,0.08);border:1px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.15);color:var(--text-dim);">
          VAR — CPU/GPU Selection, RAM, Storage
        </div>
        <div class="layer-bar" style="background:rgba(245,158,11,0.05);border:1px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.1);color:var(--text-dim);">
          VAR — Brand, Software, Support, Warranty
        </div>
        <div class="layer-bar" style="background:rgba(245,158,11,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.08);color:#555;">
          YOU — The end user who sees only the lid
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-section reveal">
      <p>Because Clevo sells B2B, five impacts hit you without you knowing why:</p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="tech-bullet" style="border-color: var(--amber);">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase mb-2" style="color:var(--amber);">Thermal Architecture</p>
        <p class="text-sm">The <strong>Clevo X170 SM-G</strong> with desktop i9-13900K + RTX 4090 uses dual-fan quad-heat-pipe. The fans are ruled by the <strong>EC</strong> — embedded controller — a microcontroller with its own real-time OS. EC locks the fan curve. Tools like ThrottleStop send commands to Windows; EC overrides them. You want a quiet studio; EC wants 4,000 RPM at 60°C.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="tech-bullet" style="border-color: var(--amber);">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase mb-2" style="color:var(--amber);">Upgradeability</p>
        <p class="text-sm">2017 <strong>P650RE</strong> — two SO-DIMM, two M.2. Tinkerer's dream. 2022 <strong>N150ZU</strong> — soldered DDR5, one accessible NVMe. Part technical — DDR5 signal integrity needs short traces and Z-height — part opacity. Clevo's datasheet says soldered, but only VARs see it. You discover it two years later.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="tech-bullet" style="border-color: var(--amber);">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase mb-2" style="color:var(--amber);">Orphan Firmware</p>
        <p class="text-sm">Clevo builds a robust BIOS but only ships updates to VARs. If your VAR pivots chassis or lacks staff, you are cut off. Critical flaws like <strong>ThunderSpy</strong> — a DMA attack on Thunderbolt that bypasses login and disk encryption via direct PCI lane access — need BIOS-level kernel DMA protection. Intel patches, Clevo patches, VAR doesn't compile it, you stay vulnerable. You can't flash generic Clevo BIOS — hardware ID mismatch bricks the board.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="tech-bullet" style="border-color: var(--amber);">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase mb-2" style="color:var(--amber);">Display Roulette</p>
        <p class="text-sm">Clevo relies on the <strong>Tcon</strong> — timing controller — between GPU and LCD. Tcon translates digital signal to row/column voltages at microsecond precision. A VAR selling "144Hz" means Tcon supports 144Hz, not that any 144Hz panel works. Wrong timing = dropped frames, no G-Sync, washed out, or black.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="tech-bullet" style="border-color: var(--amber);">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase mb-2" style="color:var(--amber);">Hidden Dependencies</p>
        <p class="text-sm"><strong>N150WZ</strong> with Linux 6.1 — <strong>ITE IT8686E Super IO</strong> chip handles sensors and fans with proprietary register layout. Mainline kernel didn't know how to talk to it, so sensors unreadable, fail-safe goes 100% fan — jet engine plus thermal throttling.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="diagram-container reveal" style="margin-top:48px;">
      <div style="position:absolute;top:0;left:0;right:0;height:2px;background:var(--amber);"></div>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider mb-4" style="color:var(--amber);">Alibaba White-Label Commoditization</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
        <div class="stat-card text-center">
          <p class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold" style="color:var(--amber);">$192</p>
          <p class="text-xs mt-1" style="color:var(--text-dim);">15.6" Intel N200</p>
          <p class="text-xs" style="color:#555;">MOQ 2 units</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-card text-center">
          <p class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold" style="color:var(--amber);">$101</p>
          <p class="text-xs mt-1" style="color:var(--text-dim);">Quad-core 14"</p>
          <p class="text-xs" style="color:#555;">MOQ 2 units</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-card text-center">
          <p class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold" style="color:var(--amber);">$10</p>
          <p class="text-xs mt-1" style="color:var(--text-dim);">MagSafe Power Bank</p>
          <p class="text-xs" style="color:#555;">per unit</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-card text-center">
          <p class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold" style="color:var(--amber);">∞</p>
          <p class="text-xs mt-1" style="color:var(--text-dim);">Brands, same box</p>
          <p class="text-xs" style="color:#555;">value → silicon + logic</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="quote-block reveal" style="border-color: var(--amber);">
      <p style="color:var(--text-dim);">The metal and plastic are commoditized. Value migrated to the silicon inside and the logic on top.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION 2: THE SILICON -->
<section class="section-block" id="sec2">
  <div class="content-wrapper relative">
    <div class="section-number" style="color: var(--cyan);">02</div>
    
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4" style="color: var(--cyan);">Layer 02 — Silicon</p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-8">The Silicon Has to Be Sovereign Too</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-section reveal">
      <p>If the box is cheap, the brain is the choke point. That's <strong>Huawei Kunpeng 920</strong>.</p>
      <p>Huawei didn't tweak a core — they went to TSMC 7-nanometer. Transistor gates a few dozen atoms wide. Built for data center and 5G.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="diagram-container reveal">
      <div style="position:absolute;top:0;left:0;right:0;height:2px;background:var(--cyan);"></div>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider mb-6" style="color:var(--cyan);">Kunpeng 920 — Chiplet Architecture (CoWoS 2.5D)</p>
      
      <div class="relative" style="max-width:420px;margin:0 auto;">
        <!-- Interposer -->
        <div style="background:rgba(6,182,212,0.05);border:1px dashed rgba(6,182,212,0.3);border-radius:8px;padding:24px;">
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] mb-3" style="color:var(--cyan);">65nm Interposer — 400 GB/s inter-die bandwidth</p>
          <div class="chiplet-grid">
            <div class="chiplet" style="background:rgba(6,182,212,0.2);border:1px solid rgba(6,182,212,0.4);color:var(--cyan);">SCCL 0</div>
            <div class="chiplet" style="background:rgba(6,182,212,0.2);border:1px solid rgba(6,182,212,0.4);color:var(--cyan);">SCCL 1</div>
            <div class="chiplet" style="background:rgba(6,182,212,0.2);border:1px solid rgba(6,182,212,0.4);color:var(--cyan);">SCCL 2</div>
            <div class="chiplet" style="background:rgba(6,182,212,0.2);border:1px solid rgba(6,182,212,0.4);color:var(--cyan);">SCCL 3</div>
            <div class="chiplet" style="background:rgba(6,182,212,0.15);border:1px solid rgba(6,182,212,0.3);color:var(--cyan);">SCCL 4</div>
            <div class="chiplet" style="background:rgba(6,182,212,0.15);border:1px solid rgba(6,182,212,0.3);color:var(--cyan);">SCCL 5</div>
            <div class="chiplet" style="background:rgba(6,182,212,0.15);border:1px solid rgba(6,182,212,0.3);color:var(--cyan);">SCCL 6</div>
            <div class="chiplet" style="background:rgba(6,182,212,0.15);border:1px solid rgba(6,182,212,0.3);color:var(--cyan);">SCCL 7</div>
            <div class="chiplet" style="background:rgba(139,92,246,0.15);border:1px solid rgba(139,92,246,0.3);color:var(--violet);grid-column:span 2;">IO Die — PCIe/Network (16nm)</div>
            <div class="chiplet" style="background:rgba(139,92,246,0.15);border:1px solid rgba(139,92,246,0.3);color:var(--violet);grid-column:span 2;">IO Die — Memory Ctrl (16nm)</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] mt-3 text-center" style="color:#555;">7nm SCCLs (expensive) + 16nm IO dies (cheap) = high yield, one chip to software</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-section reveal">
      <p><strong>But internal traffic jams:</strong></p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="tech-bullet" style="border-color: var(--cyan);">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase mb-2" style="color:var(--cyan);">L3 Cache — NUMA Partition</p>
        <p class="text-sm">Instead of shared public library, they used private <strong>NUMA</strong> mode. Private bookshelf per cluster. Hit local 4MB = <span class="highlight">36 cycles</span>. Spill over boundary = <span class="highlight">90+ cycles</span>. Two sibling cores in same cluster sharing data = <span class="highlight">80+ cycles</span>. Coherency protocol on narrow ring bus can't keep up.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="tech-bullet" style="border-color: var(--cyan);">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase mb-2" style="color:var(--cyan);">Core — TaiShan V110</p>
        <p class="text-sm">First custom 64-bit ARMv8, 4-wide out-of-order. <strong>Branch prediction:</strong> 64-entry BTB. If prediction inside BTB = <span class="highlight">1 cycle</span>. If code spills from 64KB L1 instruction cache to L2 and mispredicts = <span class="highlight">38 cycles paralyzed</span>. <strong>ALUs:</strong> 3 general, 1 multi-cycle port — integer multiply = 4 cycles waiting. <strong>TLB:</strong> 32-entry data TLB + 1024-entry L2 = <span class="highlight">11 cycles</span> on L2 lookup vs AMD Zen 2 = <span class="highlight">7 cycles</span> with 2× larger buffer.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

